1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,626
7 May 2020. Anchal, Kollam district, Kerala.

2
00:00:02,676 --> 00:00:05,799
At dawn, a mother goes to wake her daughter.

3
00:00:05,849 --> 00:00:08,724
The daughter does not wake. Mouth open, not moving.

4
00:00:08,774 --> 00:00:11,649
The doctors say she was bitten by a snake.

5
00:00:11,699 --> 00:00:14,263
And that too in a room with the AC on and the window shut.

6
00:00:14,313 --> 00:00:17,126
But one thing would not let the family sleep.

7
00:00:17,176 --> 00:00:21,420
Just two months earlier, another snake had bitten this same woman.

8
00:00:21,470 --> 00:00:24,159
Both times, her husband was right beside her.

9
00:00:24,209 --> 00:00:26,835
A man who turned a snake into a murder weapon.

10
00:00:26,885 --> 00:00:32,498
To catch him, the police tested a live cobra on a dummy.

11
00:00:32,548 --> 00:00:35,547
You will learn three things in this video.

12
00:00:35,597 --> 00:00:41,709
How the husband planned it, and how the police caught him from a single bite mark.

13
00:00:41,759 --> 00:00:44,571
And finally, what punishment the court gave.

14
00:00:44,621 --> 00:00:46,750
What happened? Watch till the end.

15
00:01:00,250 --> 00:01:03,522
This is a real case that the court has already decided.

16
00:01:03,572 --> 00:01:06,620
I am telling it based only on the judgment and news reports.

17
00:01:06,670 --> 00:01:10,900
All pictures are illustrations. They are not photographs of real people.

18
00:01:11,400 --> 00:01:14,213
The victim's name was Uthra. She was twenty-five.

19
00:01:14,263 --> 00:01:16,650
She lived with her parents in Anchal.

20
00:01:16,700 --> 00:01:19,147
Uthra had a minor disability.

21
00:01:19,197 --> 00:01:24,874
So her family wanted a caring husband with a good character.

22
00:01:24,924 --> 00:01:30,235
March 2018. Through a marriage broker, she married Sooraj S.

23
00:01:30,285 --> 00:01:33,769
Kumar, from Parakode near Adoor. He had a bank-related job.

24
00:01:33,819 --> 00:01:35,718
Sooraj's family was not rich.

25
00:01:35,768 --> 00:01:42,907
Police say Uthra's parents gave about ninety-eight sovereigns of gold, a car and cash at the wedding.

26
00:01:42,957 --> 00:01:45,709
Different reports give slightly different numbers.

27
00:01:45,759 --> 00:01:51,314
But it was not enough. According to the judgment, Sooraj's parents kept demanding more.

28
00:01:51,364 --> 00:01:57,102
Household appliances, another car, house renovation costs, and Sooraj's sister's MBA

29
00:01:57,152 --> 00:02:00,574
fees. Uthra's father paid for all of it.

30
00:02:00,624 --> 00:02:06,240
It is also said he paid Sooraj eight thousand rupees every month to look after his daughter.

31
00:02:06,290 --> 00:02:13,429
They had a son. But the judgment says Uthra's disability left Sooraj dissatisfied.

32
00:02:13,479 --> 00:02:17,449
After that, he began planning to kill her.

33
00:02:17,949 --> 00:02:22,427
From October 2019, strange searches began on Sooraj's mobile.

34
00:02:22,477 --> 00:02:24,602
Venomous snakes. Snake catchers.

35
00:02:24,652 --> 00:02:30,481
He watched Vava Suresh's YouTube videos for hours. Vava Suresh is a very famous snake catcher in Kerala.

36
00:02:30,531 --> 00:02:31,481
26 February 2020.

37
00:02:31,531 --> 00:02:38,888
He lied to another snake catcher, Suresh Kumar, saying there were rats at home, and bought a Russell's viper.

38
00:02:38,938 --> 00:02:41,475
This Suresh is not related to Vava Suresh.

39
00:02:41,525 --> 00:02:48,295
The next day, he left the snake on the staircase and asked Uthra to go upstairs and fetch his mobile.

40
00:02:48,345 --> 00:02:52,058
Uthra saw the snake and screamed. The attempt failed.

41
00:02:52,108 --> 00:02:57,702
2 March. That night Sooraj gave Uthra a sweet mixed with sleeping pills.

42
00:02:57,752 --> 00:03:00,877
When she fell asleep, he made the snake bite her leg.

43
00:03:00,927 --> 00:03:03,699
Uthra woke up screaming. She could not bear the pain.

44
00:03:03,749 --> 00:03:09,166
They took her to hospital. Sooraj said she must have been bitten outside while washing clothes.

45
00:03:09,216 --> 00:03:13,399
Uthra said she never washes clothes after dark.

46
00:03:13,899 --> 00:03:19,031
Uthra spent fifty-two days in intensive care at Pushpagiri Hospital in Thiruvalla.

47
00:03:19,081 --> 00:03:21,767
She also had a skin graft surgery.

48
00:03:21,817 --> 00:03:23,456
And here is a chilling part.

49
00:03:23,506 --> 00:03:29,568
While Uthra was fighting for her life, Sooraj was searching about cobras on his mobile.

50
00:03:29,618 --> 00:03:34,692
22 April. Uthra was discharged and, unable to walk, went to her parents' home.

51
00:03:34,742 --> 00:03:36,380
Fifteen days later, 6 May.

52
00:03:36,430 --> 00:03:44,123
Sooraj brought a cobra, bought again from Suresh, hidden in a bag inside a plastic jar, to their house.

53
00:03:44,173 --> 00:03:48,140
That night he gave Uthra juice mixed with a sedative.

54
00:03:48,190 --> 00:03:50,644
He put the snake on her. But it did not bite.

55
00:03:50,694 --> 00:03:58,387
Around two thirty in the morning, the judgment says he held the cobra's head and made it bite her left arm twice.

56
00:03:58,437 --> 00:04:03,510
He did not sleep. He washed the glass tumbler and the stick used to hold the snake.

57
00:04:03,560 --> 00:04:07,643
He also deleted the call history. In the morning, Uthra's mother found her.

58
00:04:07,693 --> 00:04:08,749
Her daughter was dead.

59
00:04:09,249 --> 00:04:15,490
Uthra's brother Vishu saw a cobra in the house, killed it and buried it on police advice.

60
00:04:15,540 --> 00:04:19,547
Sooraj said it was an accident. The snake must have come and bitten her by itself.

61
00:04:19,597 --> 00:04:23,604
But the police were suspicious. Because Uthra's body had two bite marks.

62
00:04:23,654 --> 00:04:26,426
They were two millimetres apart.

63
00:04:26,476 --> 00:04:30,659
Cobras are usually calm after eight at night.

64
00:04:30,709 --> 00:04:32,658
If one bites once, it moves away.

65
00:04:32,708 --> 00:04:39,830
Now, if you were the investigating officer, how would you prove whether a snake bit on its own, or someone made it bite?

66
00:04:39,880 --> 00:04:42,299
Pause the video and tell me in the comments.

67
00:04:42,799 --> 00:04:47,399
What the police did was extraordinary. They ran a test with a live cobra.

68
00:04:47,449 --> 00:04:54,007
Under DySP Asokan, the team laid a dummy the size of Uthra on a cot.

69
00:04:54,057 --> 00:04:56,822
They tied a piece of chicken to its arm.

70
00:04:56,872 --> 00:05:00,921
They released the cobra. It touched the dummy many times but did not bite.

71
00:05:00,971 --> 00:05:04,347
After several provocations, it bit just once.

72
00:05:04,397 --> 00:05:09,915
In that natural bite, the distance between the two fangs was one and three-quarter centimetres.

73
00:05:09,965 --> 00:05:14,932
Next, they held the snake's head and pressed it onto the chicken to make it bite.

74
00:05:14,982 --> 00:05:18,052
In those bites the distance was two to two and a half centimetres.

75
00:05:18,102 --> 00:05:21,478
On Uthra's body it was up to two point eight centimetres.

76
00:05:21,528 --> 00:05:26,189
That proved someone had opened the snake's jaw and made it bite.

77
00:05:26,239 --> 00:05:31,634
There is more. This cobra can only raise a third of its body length.

78
00:05:31,684 --> 00:05:35,061
So it could not have climbed the window ledge into the room.

79
00:05:35,111 --> 00:05:38,426
All three air vents of the room were sealed.

80
00:05:38,476 --> 00:05:40,873
They dug up the buried cobra.

81
00:05:40,923 --> 00:05:46,012
Its stomach was empty. A snake takes about seven days to digest a meal.

82
00:05:46,062 --> 00:05:49,867
That means it had been kept confined for at least seven days.

83
00:05:49,917 --> 00:05:54,089
Experts also spoke about the Russell's viper from March.

84
00:05:54,139 --> 00:05:58,555
It does not live in wet soil, and cannot climb up to an upper floor on a smooth floor.

85
00:05:58,605 --> 00:06:03,449
Locals said no viper had been seen in that area for fifteen years.

86
00:06:03,949 --> 00:06:10,600
24 May 2020. Under Crime Branch DySP Asokan, Sooraj, snake catcher Suresh and another associate were arrested.

87
00:06:10,650 --> 00:06:14,447
Suresh admitted selling both snakes to Sooraj.

88
00:06:14,497 --> 00:06:18,108
But he said he had no part in the murder plan.

89
00:06:18,158 --> 00:06:26,049
Suresh said Sooraj called him, told him not to tell anyone, and said they could call it a snake curse.

90
00:06:26,099 --> 00:06:30,020
The Kollam Chief Judicial Magistrate granted Suresh a pardon.

91
00:06:30,070 --> 00:06:35,604
He became a prosecution witness. Traces of sleeping pills were found in Uthra's urine.

92
00:06:35,654 --> 00:06:45,345
Snake searches on Sooraj's mobile, call records, sleeping pills in his car, the plastic jar that held the cobra, all of this the police presented as evidence.

93
00:06:45,395 --> 00:06:48,695
In August 2020, Sooraj's mother, sister and father were also arrested.

94
00:06:48,745 --> 00:06:52,542
The charges were conspiracy, domestic violence and destroying evidence.

95
00:06:52,592 --> 00:06:57,071
14 August 2020. A chargesheet of nearly one thousand pages was filed.

96
00:06:57,121 --> 00:07:03,399
The Forest Department also filed a separate case against Sooraj and Suresh under the Wildlife Protection Act.

97
00:07:03,899 --> 00:07:07,967
The trial was held in 2021. Vava Suresh came as a witness.

98
00:07:08,017 --> 00:07:16,076
He said that in thirty years Russell's vipers had bitten him sixteen times and cobras three hundred and forty times.

99
00:07:16,126 --> 00:07:20,828
He said a snake that bites to protect itself does not bite twice.

100
00:07:20,878 --> 00:07:26,782
It would have woken her from sleep, had she not been sedated.

101
00:07:26,832 --> 00:07:32,294
11 October 2021. The Kollam Additional Sessions Court declared Sooraj guilty.

102
00:07:32,344 --> 00:07:36,729
The charges were murder, attempt to murder, administering poison and destroying evidence.

103
00:07:36,779 --> 00:07:39,959
13 October. Judge M. Manoj announced the sentence.

104
00:07:40,009 --> 00:07:44,964
Double life imprisonment. Before that, separate terms of ten years and seven years.

105
00:07:45,014 --> 00:07:49,779
A fine of five lakh rupees. The judge said the crime was cruel and shocking.

106
00:07:49,829 --> 00:07:53,770
But he said it did not fall under the rarest of rare category for the death penalty.

107
00:07:53,820 --> 00:07:57,698
Uthra's mother Manimekhala had hoped for the death penalty.

108
00:07:57,748 --> 00:08:04,349
So she was disappointed. Sooraj's lawyer called it a moral punishment and said they would appeal.

109
00:08:04,849 --> 00:08:07,810
Uthra's son was not even three years old then.

110
00:08:07,860 --> 00:08:11,171
He does not know what happened that day.

111
00:08:11,221 --> 00:08:14,111
Here is what we should take from this case.

112
00:08:14,161 --> 00:08:16,982
One. There was no eyewitness.

113
00:08:17,032 --> 00:08:24,683
But science, the size of the bite, internet searches and the snake's stomach together brought out the truth.

114
00:08:24,733 --> 00:08:28,814
Two. Dowry. A thing that is a legal offence in India.

115
00:08:28,864 --> 00:08:32,034
And because of it, a family lost a life.

116
00:08:32,084 --> 00:08:38,195
Three. Uthra's family did not let it go as an accident. They doubted and filed a complaint.

117
00:08:38,245 --> 00:08:41,486
Without that, this case would never have come out.

118
00:08:41,536 --> 00:08:47,647
Now a question for you. In this case, Uthra's family expected the death penalty.

119
00:08:47,697 --> 00:08:53,528
The court gave double life. What do you think the punishment should be?

120
00:08:53,578 --> 00:08:57,799
Write in the comments. If you liked this video, like it.

121
00:08:57,849 --> 00:09:02,979
Subscribe to the channel. I will meet you in the next case with another mystery.

122
00:09:03,029 --> 00:09:03,399
Thank you.

